{"type":"text","timestamp":1795479771893,"sessionID":"ses_df51112b2ffe3EJKuBapwQb0Vo","part":{"id":"prt_20aef18fa002cskt1zqFaAVqv5","sessionID":"ses_df51112b2ffe3EJKuBapwQb0Vo","messageID":"msg_20aef13b1001P61NxRHi0FFKC8","type":"text","text":"Found the bug. `euros.toString()` drops trailing zeros, so `1050 / 100 = 10.5` renders as `\"10,5\"`. Let me fix it to always format with two decimals.\n\n","time":{"start":1795479771386,"end":1795479771893}}}
